    "synopsis": "La Haine (French pronunciation: [la ɛn], lit. 'Hatred'; released in the United States as Hate) is a 1995 French social thriller film written, co-edited, and directed by Mathieu Kassovitz. Starring Vincent Cassel, Hubert Koundé and Saïd Taghmaoui, the film chronicles a day and night in the lives of three friends from a poor immigrant neighbourhood in the suburbs of Paris. The title derives from a line spoken by Hubert, \"La haine attire la haine!\", translated as \"hatred breeds hatred\". Kassovitz was awarded the Best Director prize at the 1995 Cannes Film Festival.",
